.\" Adapted for NeoDarwin's acpidump, which reads the I/O Registry, 2026.
.\"
.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt ACPIDUMP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm acpidump
.Nd dump ACPI tables and ASL
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl f Ar dsdt_input
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl o Ar dsdt_output
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl T Ar table_name
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility prints the machine's ACPI tables and can dump the DSDT to a file.
In addition,
.Nm
can call
.Xr iasl 8
to disassemble AML
(ACPI Machine Language)
found in these tables and dump them as ASL
(ACPI Source Language)
to stdout.
.Pp
FreeBSD's
.Nm
reads the tables from physical memory through
.Pa /dev/mem ,
which NeoDarwin doesn't have.
NeoDarwin's ACPI platform publishes them in the I/O Registry instead, as the
.Qq ACPI Tables
property: a dictionary from each table's signature to the whole table.
A signature seen again gets a suffix, so SSDTs are
.Qq SSDT ,
.Qq SSDT-1 ,
and so on; the RSDP and the XSDT are there too.
.Nm
finds the property by searching the service plane from its root, as
.Dl ioreg -rd1 -k \(dqACPI Tables\(dq
does.
.Pp
If any Secondary System Description Table
(SSDT)
entries exist, they will also be included in the output file and disassembly.
.Pp
When invoked with the
.Fl t
flag, the
.Nm
utility prints the RSDP, the XSDT with its entries, and the common header
of every other table: Signature, Length, Revision, Checksum, OEMID,
OEM Table ID, OEM Revision, Creator ID and Creator Revision, in FreeBSD's
format.
The MCFG's allocations (base address, segment group and bus range) are
also printed.
FreeBSD decodes the bodies of further tables (FADT, MADT, SPCR and others);
NeoDarwin's
.Nm
doesn't yet.
As in FreeBSD, the FACS and the DSDT are printed after the FADT.
The registry doesn't keep the XSDT's order, so the FADT comes first and the
other tables follow in order of signature.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Concatenate the DSDT and the SSDTs into a single image, disassemble it into
ASL with
.Pa /usr/sbin/iasl Fl d ,
and print the results to stdout.
.It Fl f Ar dsdt_input
Load the DSDT from the specified file instead of the I/O Registry, for
.Fl d .
.It Fl h
Display usage and exit.
.It Fl o Ar dsdt_output
Store the DSDT, with the SSDTs' bodies appended and its checksum redone,
in the specified file.
.It Fl s
Like
.Fl d ,
but disassemble the DSDT and each SSDT separately.
.It Fl t
Print the tables as described above.
.It Fl T Ar table_name
Print only the tables with the four-character signature
.Ar table_name .
.It Fl v
Enable verbose messages.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/sbin/iasl
.It Pa /usr/sbin/iasl
The ACPICA compiler and disassembler,
.Fl d
and
.Fl s .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print the tables:
.Pp
.Dl # acpidump -t
.Pp
Disassemble the DSDT and SSDTs:
.Pp
.Dl # acpidump -d > my.asl
.Pp
Save the DSDT to a file:
.Pp
.Dl # acpidump -o my.dsdt
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr iasl 8 ,
.Xr ioreg 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Fx 5.0 .
NeoDarwin's, over the I/O Registry, is new.
